sentences.t:
Illam, summa super labentem culmina tecti,
cernimus Idaea claram se condere silva
signantemque vias;

sentences.l:
Her, over the highest ridges of the roof gliding,
we see, bright, herself to hide in the Idaean wood
and marking the ways;

sentences.t:
Haec fatus, latos umeros subiectaque colla
veste super fulvique insternor pelle leonis,
succedoque oneri;

sentences.l:
These things having said, broad shoulders and bent-under neck
with a garment over and of a tawny lion with the skin I am spread over,
and I go under the load;

For pathless places in my course
while I follow, and from the known region of the streets I depart,
alas, to me wretched, my wife whether by fate taken away Creusa
stopped, or went astray from the way, or weary sat down,
uncertain;

sentences.t:
Nec prius amissam respexi animumque reflexi,
quam tumulum antiquae Cereris sedemque sacratam
venimus;

sentences.l:
Nor before her lost did I look back or bend back my mind,
than the mound of ancient Ceres and the sacred seat
we came to;

Hither from every side Trojan treasure
from burned shrines snatched, and the tables of the gods,
and mixing-bowls of solid gold, and captive raiment
is heaped;

sentences.t:
Iamque iugis summae surgebat Lucifer Idae
ducebatque diem, Danaique obsessa tenebant
limina portarum, nec spes opis ulla dabatur;

sentences.l:
And now over the ridges of highest Ida was rising the Morning Star
and was leading the day, and the Danaans the beset
thresholds of the gates were holding, nor hope of help any was being given;
